text:
claim :- Donald Trump delivered the largest tax cuts in American history. , Evidence :- Three tax bills have been larger than that of Donald Trump , This tax cut is the 8th largest as a percent of Gross Domestic Product (GDP) since 1918 and the 4th largest in inflation-adjusted dollars. , Three tax bills have been larger: American Taxpayer Relief Act of 2012 (enacted in 2013); 
Tax Relief, Unemployment Insurance Reauthorization, and Job Creation Act of 2010 and
Economic Recovery Tax Act of 1981 ,

claim :- South Africa has “expertise in the development and trial of a range of vaccines” , Evidence :- There are institutions in South Africa with adequate facilities that deals in vaccine value chain, from development to manufacturing and distribution.  , The American Society for Microbiology Journals published online on April 3, 2019, a research paper entitled Prime-Boost Immunizations with DNA, Modified Vaccinia Virus Ankara, and Protein-Based Vaccines Elicit Robust HIV-1 Tier 2 Neutralizing Antibodies against the CAP256 Superinfecting Virus written by authors from South Africa's
Institute of Infectious Disease and Molecular Medicine, Faculty of Health Science, University of Cape Town, Cape Town, South Africa;
Division of Medical Virology, Department of Pathology, University of Cape Town, Cape Town, South Africa;
Centre for HIV and STIs, National Institute for Communicable Diseases of the National Health Laboratory Service, Johannesburg, South Africa;
Faculty of Health Sciences, University of the Witwatersrand, Johannesburg, South Africa;
Centre for the AIDS Programme of Research in South Africa (CAPRISA), University of KwaZulu-Natal, Congella, South Africa;
Biopharming Research Unit, Department of Molecular and Cell Biology, University of Cape Town, Cape Town, South Africa , Headquartered in Cape Town, the Biovac Institute is the result of a partnership formed with the South African government in 2003 to establish vaccine manufacturer in South Africa. The company partners with various organisations across the vaccine value chain, from development to manufacturing and distribution.. , We have developed a technology package for the manufacture of Haemophilus influenzae type b (Hib) conjugate vaccine. To date, this has been transferred to two international vaccine manufacturers. One of our partners has successfully commercialised a pentavalent vaccine containing Diphtheria, Tetanus, Pertussis, Hepatitis B, Haemophilus influenzae b (DTP-HepB-Hib) using our conjugate Hib vaccine technology. The second partner has started clinical trials. ,

claim :- Sarah Sachin Pilot attacks Gehlot in a tweet saying that even "big magicians" will start sweating when they turn to Delhi. , Evidence :- She did not tweet such a claim. , Please don't use tweets from here to file stories. This is a FAKE twitter account. 

Surprised to see tweets from this account making it to mainstream news and agency stories. 
@TwitterIndia please take note , ... the account of ‘Sarah Sachin Pilot’ was not verified. ,

claim :- “India let 65 lakh tonne of grain go waste in four months, even as the poor went hungry. , Evidence :- Although some food was wasted due to floods whilst on transit, it was a gross misinterpretation  , Food Corporation of India , Misleading news published in 
@scroll_in
 on Food Grains gone waste, FCI's rebuttal attached , They added a letter. , They explained that the statistics quoted in the article were a gross misinterpretation of the facts, that the article had claimed that a large amount of grain had gone to waste, when it was simply in transit. They said the figure of 71.8 lakh metric tonne of wasted stock was 'imaginary' and the amount was 1,930 metric tonnes and that was largely due to  'natural calamities like floods' ,

claim :- Madagascar’s President Andry Rajoelina called on African nations to leave the World Health Organization (WHO). , Evidence :- According to the source, the Madagascar’s President Andry Rajoelina did not threaten to pull Madagascar from WHO or call on African countries to leave WHO. , In an interview on May 11, 2020 -- days before the claims started circulating on Facebook -- Rajoelina criticised the WHO for refusing to endorse his herbal remedy. He did not threaten to pull Madagascar from WHO or call on African countries to leave WHO. , Yes he tweeted:

"Successful exchange with @DrTedros who commends #Madagascar’s efforts in the fight against #Covid19.
@WHO will sign a confidentiality clause on the formulation of the #CovidOrganics and will support the clinical observations process in #Africa." ,

claim :- Neem leaves can cure the novel coronavirus and relieve its symptoms. , Evidence :- From the evidence below, it looks like Neem leaves cannot cure the COVID-19 virus or relieve its symptoms. Neem leaves can be used to treat skin conditions like eczema. , Neem leaves are medium to large in size and elongated to oblong in shape, averaging 20-40 centimeters in length. The vibrant green leaves are smooth and glossy with sharp, serrated edges. Neem leaves grow on the branches of neem trees in groups of two, and each branch produces around eight groupings. Neem leaves are extremely bitter and have a grassy taste and aroma when torn. Neem trees also grow white, fragrant flowers and yellow, olive-like fruit that has a bittersweet pulp. , the best-established and most widely recognized uses are based on its merits as a general antiseptic. Neem preparations are reportedly efficacious against a variety of skin diseases, septic sores, and infected burns. The leaves, applied in the form of poultices or decoctions, are also recommended for boils, ulcers, and eczema. , The attached Malay-language  infographic translates to English as:
“The usage of neem leaves for COVID-19 outbreak

“Myths 
- Traditionally, neem leaves are used for various fever and infections; 
- Can be used on humans to treat COVID-19 outbreak; 
- Can stimulate immune cells or the body’s self-defense; 
- No side effects and safe for usage.

“Facts 
- No clear record on required dosage; 
- For now, there are only studies on cells (in vitro) and animals (in vivo) that have been carried on the hepatitis C virus, dengue and polio. There is no study on the coronavirus that causes COVID-19;
- No studies on the effectiveness on the human’s immune system except study on cells (in-vitro) that focuses on the bacteria and not virus;
- Safety data concerning all parts of the plant shows: 
Adults: May be safe if taken in a short period of time and in low dosage quantity;       
Children: Not safe because can cause seizures, vomiting, coma, loss of consciousness and can cause death;
Pregnant women: Can cause miscarriage”. ,

claim :- Covid-19 is very similar to the seasonal flu with U.S mortality rates just above 0.1 percent and students are being punished and academies easily incapacitated by the common cold. , Evidence :- Evidence denies the mortality rates and the similarities between the flu and Covid-19. , NO:
COVID-19 is novel, or new. That means there's no vaccine, and it's unclear how it will manifest;
This strain of coronavirus appears to infect two to 2.5 people versus 1.3 with the flu, so coronavirus seems to be about twice as contagious as the flu;
Some 20% of coronavirus patients are in serious enough condition to go to the hospital, 10 times the number who wind up in the hospital because of the flu;
Hospital stays for the coronavirus are twice as long as for the flu;
About 8% of people get the flu every year. Some estimates are 25% to 50%, possibly up to 80%, could get the coronavirus without drastic actions being taken by individuals, states and municipalities and the federal government;
The coronavirus could be 10 times deadlier than the flu — about 0.1% who get flu die. It's estimated that about 1% of those who have gotten coronavirus have died from it;
There are treatments for the flu. There are no approved treatments for the coronavirus, despite the president's optimism for certain drugs, which are untested for coronavirus to this point; and
The flu tends to wane in warm weather, but it's too soon to count on that for coronavirus, which is thriving in warm, tropical places. , no its believed to be 1%

The coronavirus could be 10 times deadlier than the flu — about 0.1% who get flu die. It's estimated that about 1% of those who have gotten coronavirus have died from it; ,

claim :- US has many health care plans which are 60 to 65 percent less expensive than Obamacare. , Evidence :- The answers and sources show there are many different health care plans but they do not have any evidence to say they are cheaper so the claim can not be supported or refuted. , In the Affordable Care Act marketplace , The Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act of 1996 (HIPAA) [1] added title XXVII to the Public Health Service Act (PHS Act), part 7 to the Employee Retirement Income Security Act of 1974 (ERISA), and Chapter 100 to the Internal Revenue Code (the Code), providing portability and nondiscrimination rules with respect to health coverage. These provisions of the PHS Act, ERISA, and the Code were later augmented by other laws, including the Mental Health Parity Act of 1996,[2] the Paul Wellstone and Pete Domenici Mental Health Parity and Addiction Equity Act of 2008,[3] the Newborns' and Mothers' Health Protection Act,[4] the Women's Health and Cancer Rights Act,[5] the Genetic Information Nondiscrimination Act of 2008,[6] the Children's Health Insurance Program Reauthorization Act of 2009,[7] Michelle's Law,[8] and the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act, as amended by the Health Care and Education Reconciliation Act of 2010 (PPACA).[9] , Estimating the actuarial value of such products is challenging because the scope of coverage is so varied and
because coverage generally completely excludes services
for any preexisting condition ,

claim :- Iihan Omar tweeted "There is no way to overstate how ASHAMED I am to be called an 'American'. We need every world leader to rise up and demand that someone stops Trump from starting a catastrophic war with Iran." THE TIME FOR VIOLENCE IS NOW! #NoWarWithIran , Evidence :- From the 2nd QA it is evident that the account is fake, Therefore the claim is refuetd , The claim tweet appears to have been created by modifying the text in a real tweet, which reads as ; There is no way to overstate how dangerous this is. 

We need every voice to rise up and demand that Congress stop Trump from starting a catastrophic war with Iran. , A fake Twitter account pretending to be Fox News posted a fake tweet from 
@IlhanMN (Ilhan Omar) ,

claim :- Every month 17.5 million social grants are provided to South Africans. , Evidence :- The sources proved that each month around 17.5 million is given in social grants to South Africans. , South African Social Security Agency (SASSA) , By the
end of March 2018, there were 17 509 995 social grants in payment,
including the Grant-in-Aid. , The figure is a total for each month, ,

claim :- Kamala Harris say criminals and illegals are better than U.S. servicemen. , Evidence :- The claim is refuted as the answers show that Harris did not say the claim and the quote has been changed. , Today I’m thinking of the fathers who can’t be with their children because they were ripped from their sons and daughters at the border. The fathers who can’t celebrate today because they can’t afford bail. The fathers who are deployed. Don’t forget them. , David Harris Jr. , As the origin for the claim is based off the this tweet of Kamala Harris;

"Today I’m thinking of the fathers who can’t be with their children because they were ripped from their sons and daughters at the border. The fathers who can’t celebrate today because they can’t afford bail. The fathers who are deployed. Don’t forget them."

And there is no connection between the claim and the tweet. , Article spinning is a writing technique used in search engine optimization (SEO), and other applications, which creates what appears to be new content from what already exists. Content spinning works by replacing specific words, phrases, sentences, or even entire paragraphs with any number of alternate versions to provide a slightly different variation with each spin - also known as Rogeting. ,

claim :- "Kenya has been ranked 85th globally in e-commerce uptake.” , Evidence :- Kenya ranks at 89th of 151 countries in the 2018 UNCTAD B2C E-commerce Index - not 85th.  , The figure comes from the 2018 UN Conference on Trade and Development (UNCTAD) Business -to-consumer E-commerce index. The 2018 UNCTAD B2C E-commerce Index, measures an economy’s preparedness to 
support online shopping. , The 2018 UNCTAD B2C E-commerce Index has expanded its coverage to include 151 economies, up seven 
from the 2017 edition. , Kenya is ranked 89th of 151 countries. ,

claim :- In 2018, US drug prices  declined for the first time in 46 years. , Evidence :- Contrary to the claim there was price increase for drugs  , 0.4 , 0.1 , 0.6 , 0.4 , For the first seven months of 2018, there were 96 price hikes for every price cut. , Prescription drug spending growth is
then projected to further accelerate to 4.6 percent in 2019, because of faster utilization growth
from both existing and new drugs, as well as a modest increase in drug price growth. , Drug prices rose moderately in 2018, therefore drug spending is going to rise as well, partly for this reason. ,

claim :- Over ninety per cent of those who died during the Troubles in Northern Ireland were killed by paramilitaries. , Evidence :- Missing evidence: 
- no explanation in 2nd QA as to whether the Troubles referred to in the claim is the same as the Irish Civil War in 1969 (not common knowledge); 
- no evidence to support whether 90% of the over 3500 people that died during the Troubles (referred to in the 2nd QA) were people killed by paramilitaries. , No answer could be found. , More than 3,500 people died during The Troubles. ,

claim :- Cyril Ramaphosa retorted to Donald Trump’s  2018 comments on land reform in South Africa on Twitter , Evidence :- The posted tweet in reply to Donald Trump was not from Cyril Ramaphosa's twitter account  , "I have asked Secretary of State
@SecPompeo
to closely study the South Africa land and farm seizures and expropriations and the large scale killing of farmers. “South African Government is now seizing land from white farmers" , I have asked @GenBheki_Cele to closely study the USA mass shootings and large killings of unarmed civilians. "USA Government is now killing unarmed African Americans" , It does not appear on their offical account and it looks like the tweet in the screenshot was taken from someone posing as Ramaphosa online. Alternatively, it’s possible that they used an online generator to produce the post. ,

claim :- Iain Duncan Smith gets free stationery as a financial benefit for being an MP in the UK House of Commons. , Evidence :- The UK House of Commons updated version of the Green Book grants such Expenses. , IPSA will not pay claims for any of the following:
a. alcoholic drinks;
b. stationery provided by the House of Commons;
c. newsletters;
d. funding of any material, other than websites, that contains a party political logo or
emblem; or
e. personal accountancy or tax advice. , Equipment and supplies for the office or surgery - including computers, printers, faxes, photocopiers, desks, stationery, phone bills, some postage costs (in addition to AOE, MPs can also claim for a certain amount of Commons stationery and pre-paid envelopes) ,

claim :- U.S., Germany and France have no educational requirement for the office of President. , Evidence :- The question-answer pairs establish the requirements for becoming President in the countries in the claim, and there is no mention of educational requirement in the answers. , No Person except a natural born Citizen, or a Citizen of the United States, at the time of the Adoption of this Constitution, shall be eligible to the Office of President; neither shall any person be eligible to that Office who shall not have attained to the Age of thirty five Years, and been fourteen Years a Resident within the United States. , The Federal President shall be elected by the Federal Convention without debate. Any German who is entitled to vote in Bundestag elections and has attained the age of forty may be elected. , the French constitution states that a candidate for a presidential election is required to:

be a French citizen;
have attained the age of 18 years;
be qualified to vote;
not be ineligible by reasons of criminal conviction or judicial decision;
and have a bank account. ,
